WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.710
One scene. 100 MB.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.790
1.2 KB.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.470
Satellites are dumb cameras.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.740
They shoot 100 MB of ocean,

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.810
then beam every byte home.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.710
Meet the Orbital Scene Preprocessor.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.560
A satellite that thinks before it speaks.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.650
Six spectral bands, not three.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.090
Shortwave infrared sees through haze,

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.290
and metal lights up against water.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.980
Detected on board.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.360
Then it sends a brief, not a photo.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.780
100 MB, down to 1.2 KB.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.460
On the ground, one Command Centre shows every pass.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.780
A tactical map, and a live intelligence feed.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.730
ORION retrieves, remembers, reasons.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.940
Rules decide.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.760
Orange or red? The alert goes out.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.810
Unsure? Ask the satellite to look again.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.840
A judge checks every alert for hallucinations.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.490
Don't downlink the ocean.

